{
  "name": "wall_crouch_slide",
  "note": "(anim-rework S5 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) Back to the wall, crouched slide: CT's side-on crouch-walk along the wall (the posed frame: forward is the travel, the wall on the LEFT; mirrored for the other side): the crouch walk's legs (short steps of about 42 cm, knees 80-94 deg over the toes, the hips about 23 cm down, a 2 cm bob, feet near the line), the trunk about 45 deg over the knees (pelvis 22, chest 40); the right hand stays on the right knee through the slide (the arm keyed to the knee's mean place; the game's KNEE_HAND IK holds the contact as the knee moves), the left hand low by the shin, the head up along the travel. Not mirrored (8 keys: the legs alternate, the hands keep their sides). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward; wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. Holstered arms; with a weapon drawn the arms stay procedural. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
